S5a: verify review.summary:
I reviewed the diff 328a39b..963ed0f in /home/user/wt-core and ran all gates. fmt, clippy -D warnings (the workspace lints include pedantic and nursery) and RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc are clean. cargo test --workspace passes: 483 tests in 41 binaries. Logs are in SCRATCH/verify/s5/diff/. Most claimed fixes hold against many variants: 1a, 1b, 1c, 2a, 3c, 4a, 4b, 6b. The empty_at spec change has every checklist step.

The 6a change has two blockers. The W0313 check of locals now depends on abort edges, and those edges are incomplete. W0313 now misses three shapes that base reported, and each one faults at runtime ('no handler'):
- an abort to an outer handle's end (nest_abort.wf);
- a clause inside a clause (cic_clo.wf);
- a stored closure run by a callee (stored_abort.wf).

The abort-edge fix also misses the clause-in-clause shape for linear values and references outside the body (cic_lin.wf leaks a Tx, cic_ref.wf prints <dangling>).

The other majors:
- new W0405 false positives after a Fail or user handler around a `scope`: the abort edge skips the scope's task end, but the runtime cancels and waits for the tasks;
- a W0204 false positive for a function that returns an operation result;
- op_refs does not rebase `lent`, so an op-result reference given to a function parameter misses W0301;
- 3a misses a generic item given as a function value, which then aborts while it holds a linear value. ADR 0007 still claims 'no known gap'.

The minors are wrong-location reporting, conservative false positives and quadratic join handling. Repro files are in SCRATCH/verify/s5/diff/p/.
